DAY 60 - PART A: THEORY
CSI Drivers and StorageClasses: How Storage Plugins Work
Time: 40 minutes
==================================================================

1. CSI ARCHITECTURE
-------------------
A CSI driver has two parts:
  Controller plugin (Deployment)   talks to the storage system:
                                   CreateVolume, DeleteVolume,
                                   ControllerPublish (attach),
                                   CreateSnapshot, Expand
  Node plugin (DaemonSet)          on each node: NodeStage (format,
                                   mount to a global path),
                                   NodePublish (bind-mount into the pod)

Kubernetes "sidecar" containers next to the driver translate API
objects into CSI calls:
  external-provisioner   PVC -> CreateVolume -> PV
  external-attacher      VolumeAttachment -> ControllerPublish
  external-resizer       PVC size change -> Expand
  external-snapshotter   VolumeSnapshot -> CreateSnapshot
  node-driver-registrar  registers the node plugin with the kubelet
  livenessprobe


2. API OBJECTS
--------------
  CSIDriver          driver capabilities (attach required? fsGroup?)
  CSINode            which drivers are on each node + limits (max
                     volumes per node)
  StorageClass       provisioner: <driver name> + parameters
  VolumeAttachment   "attach volume X to node Y" (block drivers)
  VolumeSnapshotClass / VolumeSnapshot / VolumeSnapshotContent


3. THE FULL LIFECYCLE
---------------------
  PVC created -> external-provisioner -> CreateVolume -> PV bound
  pod scheduled -> VolumeAttachment -> attach (cloud API)
  kubelet -> NodeStage (format ext4/xfs, mount) -> NodePublish (bind
             into pod's volume dir) -> container starts
  pod deleted -> unpublish -> unstage -> detach
  PVC deleted -> reclaimPolicy Delete -> DeleteVolume


4. RWX WITH NFS
---------------
csi-driver-nfs creates a sub-directory per PV on an existing NFS
server; many pods on many nodes can mount it read-write. Cloud
equivalents: EFS CSI, Azure Files, Filestore.


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- Controller plugin (create/attach) + node plugin (mount).
- Sidecars translate Kubernetes objects into CSI calls.
- CSIDriver, CSINode, VolumeAttachment show what's happening.
